>> title: Spicy Lamb Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: lamb, basmati, eggplant, spiced, skillet, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: spicy lamb bowl, lamb bowl, ground lamb bowl, spiced lamb and rice bowl, mediterranean lamb bowl, rice bowl, grain bowl, power bowl
>> pairs-with: ras-el-hanout, tzatziki, pomegranate-molasses
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.1: Spread the lamb thin across a hot dry pan and leave it alone. Stirred early it steams grey in its own fat.
>> step.2: simmer 35 min, rest 10 min
>> step.3: fry 8 min, undisturbed, until it crusts
>> step.4: crumble it, fry 2 min with the spice
>> step.5: roast 450°F (230°C) 25 min
>> step.6: build it, lamb and eggplant over the rice

Ground lamb crisps rather than browns if you spread it thin across a hot dry pan and leave it alone until the underside sets.

Simmer @brown basmati rice{1 1/2%cups}(280 g; rinsed) in @water{2 1/2%cups}(590 mL) with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} covered ~simmer{35%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat.

Fry @ground lamb{1%lb}(450 g) spread thin across a hot dry #skillet{} ~fry{8%min}, undisturbed, until the underside is crusted and brown.

Break @&(~1)lamb{} up and fry it with @ras el hanout{1%Tbs}, @tomato paste{1%Tbs}, @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} ~fry{2%min}, until the paste darkens and coats every piece.

Roast @eggplant{1%large}(700 g; in 1-inch cubes) tossed with @olive oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL) and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} at 450°F (230°C) ~roast{25%min}, until it collapses and browns at the edges.

Spoon @&(~4)basmati{} into four bowls, pile @&(~2)spiced lamb{} and @&(~1)roasted eggplant{} over it, and finish with @red onion{1/2}(sliced paper thin), @red wine vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @mint{1/4%cup}(torn) and @plain yogurt{1/2%cup}(120 mL).
